154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (A Mini Search Engine is a software application that helps users search and retrieve information from a collection of documents efficiently. It uses Data Structures and Algorithms to organize and process data for faster searching. The system creates an index of keywords, allowing quick access to relevant documents based on user queries. By using techniques such as Hash Maps and Inverted Indexes, the search process becomes more efficient. This project demonstrates the practical application of DSA concepts in information retrieval. It provides accurate and faster search results while reducing search time. The Mini Search Engine is a simple model that helps understand how real-world search engines work.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
