161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (Several studies have shown that efficient information retrieval systems rely on Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) to improve search performance. Techniques such as HashMaps and Inverted Indexes are widely used to organize keywords and enable faster document retrieval. Traditional search methods are slower for large datasets, whereas indexed search significantly reduces search time. Modern search engines use similar indexing and ranking techniques to provide accurate results. This project adopts these fundamental concepts to develop a simple and efficient Mini Search Engine for quick keyword-based document searching.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
